{:edb/db-before-t 2605 :edb/db-after-t 2606 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535918 50 #inst "2026-10-09T10:37:15.148Z" 13194139535918 true] [17592186171961 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374297 13194139535918 true] [17592186171961 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374311 13194139535918 true] [17592186171962 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374304 13194139535918 true] [17592186171963 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374318 13194139535918 true] [17592186171963 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374325 13194139535918 true] [17592186171963 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374332 13194139535918 true] [17592186171963 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374339 13194139535918 true] [17592186171964 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374346 13194139535918 true] [17592186171964 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374353 13194139535918 true] [17592186172559 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535918 true] [17592186172559 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072015/assets/dcee145044fe79dc7f4d07c3c4c1248df358cd8eda7a173cd8d4641f13404122.png)\n\nConsider the function $f:X\\to Y$ given by the mapping diagram shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The domain of $f$ is ${0,1,2,3}$\n- The codomain of $f$ is ${0,-1}$\n- The range of $f$ is ${0,-1}$" 13194139535918 true] [17592186172559 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3334/Source/Images/q-96123.png)\n\nConsider the function $f: X → Y$ given by the mapping diagram shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. The domain of $f$ is ${0, 1, 2, 3}$\n2. The codomain of $f$ is ${0,-1}$\n3. The range of $f$ is ${0,-1}$" 13194139535918 false] [17592186172559 1145 "The notation $f:X\\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nThe range of $f$ is the subset of the codomain that contains all values $y\\in Y$ that are mapped to by at least one element $x\\in X.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect our diagram:\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X={0,1,2,3},$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y={0,-1,-2},$\n\n- the range of $f$ is ${0,-1},$ the subset of elements of $Y$ that have at least one incoming arrow.\n\nAs a result, statements I and III are true, while statement II is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer \"I and III only.\"" 13194139535918 true] [17592186172570 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535918 true] [17592186172570 1100 "Which of the following is the correct symbolic notation for the sentence given below?\n\n*\"The function $f$ maps the interval from $-1$ to $1$ exclusive to the set $Y.$\"*" 13194139535918 true] [17592186172570 1100 "Which of the following is the correct symbolic notation for the sentence given below?\n\n> *\"The function $f$ maps the interval from $-1$ to $1$ exclusive to the set $Y$.\"*" 13194139535918 false] [17592186172570 1145 "The sentence *\"The function $f$ maps the interval from $-1$ to $1$ exclusive to the set $Y$\"* is equivalent to the following symbolic notation:\n\n$\\,$ $f:(-1,1)\\to Y$\n\nHere, the domain of $f$ is $(-1,1),$ and the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$" 13194139535918 true] [17592186302388 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039287/assets/740d578e554cd61bc733079c32c063d41ab4d9dcc775d36f7080ee8e5aa5a622.png)\n\nConsider the function $f:X\\to Y$ given by the mapping diagram shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The domain of $f$ is ${5,10,15}$\n- The codomain of $f$ is ${5,10,12,13,14,15}$\n- The range of $f$ is ${12,13,14}$" 13194139535918 false] [17592186302388 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072015/assets/740d578e554cd61bc733079c32c063d41ab4d9dcc775d36f7080ee8e5aa5a622.png)\n\nConsider the function $f:X\\to Y$ given by the mapping diagram shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The domain of $f$ is ${5,10,15}$\n- The codomain of $f$ is ${5,10,12,13,14,15}$\n- The range of $f$ is ${12,13,14}$" 13194139535918 true] [17592186374297 1017 #edb/ref 17592186374298 13194139535918 true] [17592186374297 1089 "q-104781" 13194139535918 true] [17592186374297 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535918 true] [17592186374297 1100 "Which of the following functions has the domain $[-2,2]?$\n\n- $p:[-2,2]\\to (-2,2)$\n- $r:[-2,2]\\to {-2,2}$\n- $q:Z\\to [-2,2]$" 13194139535918 true] [17592186374297 1113 #uuid "1fd3104e-7952-590e-9c92-6b60840f5744" 13194139535918 true] [17592186374297 1145 "The notation $f:X\\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our functions.\n\n- The domain of $p$ is $[-2,2],$ the interval from $-2$ to $2$ (including $-2$ and $2$).\n\n- The domain of $q$ is $[-2,2],$ the interval from $-2$ to $2$ (including $-2$ and $2$).\n\n- The domain of $r$ is $Z,$ the set of integers.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139535918 true] [17592186374298 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374299 13194139535918 true] [17592186374298 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374300 13194139535918 true] [17592186374298 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374301 13194139535918 true] [17592186374298 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374302 13194139535918 true] [17592186374298 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374303 13194139535918 true] [17592186374298 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535918 true] [17592186374298 1041 "selection" 13194139535918 true] [17592186374298 1104 #edb/ref 17592186374302 13194139535918 true] [17592186374298 1110 #uuid "1751ae7c-09bc-52a4-b280-12b5074667b0" 13194139535918 true] [17592186374299 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139535918 true] [17592186374299 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535918 true] [17592186374299 1111 #uuid "57372209-b4fc-57c3-bd68-b4d674865369" 13194139535918 true] [17592186374300 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535918 true] [17592186374300 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535918 true] [17592186374300 1111 #uuid "8caf0aa7-91d8-5148-a790-ec43ff6